# Testing Rules

## Coverage Requirements
- Minimum 80% coverage enforced in CI — PR blocked if below
- Every new function gets a unit test in the same PR
- Every API endpoint gets an integration test
- Critical paths (ping dedup, eRPC scoring, TCPA check): 100% coverage

## Go Testing
- Use testify for assertions (require.NoError, assert.Equal)
- testcontainers-go for real PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka in tests
- Never mock the database — test against real containers
- Test concurrent ping ingestion with t.Parallel() and goroutines
- Benchmark tests for hot path functions (go test -bench=.)

## TypeScript Testing
- Jest for unit tests
- testcontainers for integration tests with real DB
- supertest for API endpoint testing
- Never mock PostgreSQL or Redis — use real containers

## Test Naming
- Go: TestFunctionName_Scenario_ExpectedResult
- TypeScript: describe('FunctionName') → it('should do X when Y')

## What Must Be Tested
- Ping deduplication with concurrent identical pings
- eRPC scoring formula with known inputs and expected outputs
- TCPA compliance check blocking behavior on DNC match
- Tenant isolation: tenant A cannot read tenant B data
- Graceful degradation when external service (Deepgram, OpenAI) is down
- Webhook signature verification — valid and invalid signatures

## Edge Cases Always Test
- Empty input arrays and null values
- Maximum payload sizes
- Expired JWTs and invalid API keys
- Concurrent requests to same resource
- Service unavailability (circuit breaker behavior)